{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659846",
      "title": "When NOT To Lift State Up",
      "sourceHash": "96a9f395cbac20befa6c587a87b0d88f1041f0a6665c1cc533dd8973cb3cfa17",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "So at this point we are pretty much done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "with that game.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 8.19,
          "en": "There's just one thing that would be nice to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.19,
          "end": 13.19,
          "en": "If we win here, we're currently saying \"X won\" or \"O won.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "And that's, of course, okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 18.179,
          "en": "and we know what's meant by that, but it would be nicer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.179,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "if instead we would be showing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "the name of the player who won, so Player One or Player Two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 29.493,
          "en": "or if we edit this name, the edited name, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.08,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "Now this, of course, means that we need information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "about the player names in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "because that is where we are deriving the winner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "And at the moment the player name information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 47.37,
          "en": "is stored inside of the player component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "That's where we're editing and storing the player name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 52.74,
          "en": "And we're not sharing this name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.74,
          "end": 56.13,
          "en": "with any other part of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.13,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "So, hence, we need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "that we get those player names out of the player component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 62.133,
          "en": "into the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.27,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "Now you could think that you wanna lift the state up again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 70.65,
          "en": "Maybe this player name state that you wanna lift it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.65,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "out of this player component into the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "But that would be wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "It would be wrong because this player name state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 82.86,
          "en": "is actually used to update this input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.86,
          "end": 84.96000000000001,
          "en": "on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "And if we would move it out of the player component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 90.53999999999999,
          "en": "that would mean that the entire app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "is reevaluated on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "which also means that the entire game board",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 99.84,
          "en": "is reevaluated on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.84,
          "end": 103.8,
          "en": "And that's really redundant and not what we want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.8,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "In addition, lifting this player name state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 110.25,
          "en": "out of the player component also, of course, would be tricky",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.25,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "because we're using this player component twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.893,
          "en": "and every component should manage its own name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "So, therefore, the player component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 121.47,
          "en": "should actually stay the way it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "Here, instead, I simply want to add a new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 129.063,
          "en": "to my app component here, with useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "where I store the currently set player names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "And this state here could be an array with the two names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 141.873,
          "en": "like Player One and Player Two initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.92000000000002,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "But since these player names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "are tightly coupled to their symbols,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "I think it makes more sense to use an object here as a map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "so to say, where we have the key X",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.19,
          "end": 157.59,
          "en": "and the value for that key is Player One",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.59,
          "end": 162.59,
          "en": "and the key O for the second player and that's Player Two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.75,
          "end": 165.36,
          "en": "And then, of course, we can and should destructure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.36,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "this array we get back from useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 170.19,
          "en": "And here we got our players",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.19,
          "end": 173.403,
          "en": "and a set players state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.472,
          "end": 178.409,
          "en": "Now set players should be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.409,
          "end": 183.409,
          "en": "whenever we click this save button in the player component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "Not on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "but only when we save a change to the player name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "So, therefore, of course, in this app component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 197.49,
          "en": "we should add a new function maybe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.49,
          "end": 199.69,
          "en": "which could be named handlePlayerNameChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.48,
          "end": 204.93,
          "en": "because that's, in the end, what we wanna React to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 209.31,
          "en": "And here I expect to get the symbol of the player",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.31,
          "end": 214.31,
          "en": "for whom the name changed and the new name as arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 219.99,
          "en": "And then we can call setPlayers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.99,
          "end": 223.14,
          "en": "So this state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.14,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "of this newly added state, which has this shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 231.12,
          "en": "And I wanna update my state based on my old state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "because, of course, only one name of one player changes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 237.93,
          "en": "and I don't wanna lose the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.93,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "and information for the other player.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 245.78,
          "en": "Therefore, in the end here, I get my previous players",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.45,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "and I'll return a new object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 253.56,
          "en": "which will be my new player's state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 258.363,
          "en": "where I'll spread my old player's object into,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "so that I start by again setting both the X and O property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.39300000000003,
          "en": "to the respective old player names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 269.16,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "But I will then overwrite one of these two properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "The property which I get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 278.46,
          "en": "with help of that symbol parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.46,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "We can do this by using this JavaScript syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 285.54,
          "en": "where we dynamically set a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.54,
          "end": 288.27,
          "en": "with this square bracket syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.27,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "so that's standard JavaScript, not React specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 295.77,
          "en": "And we set this property, which is either X or Y,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 295.77,
          "end": 299.313,
          "en": "depending on what's stored in symbol, to the new name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.77,
          "end": 305.43,
          "en": "So I use this approach to ensure that I keep the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 305.43,
          "end": 308.19,
          "en": "and symbol of the player that's not changing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 308.19,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "and I'm then just overriding the name for the symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 314.433,
          "en": "of the player that was changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 315.42,
          "end": 318.123,
          "en": "So that's how we could update the player's data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}